---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '../data/site';

const email = LEGAL.contactEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  path="/refunds/"
  lede="How billing, cancellation, and refunds work for your DummyLead subscription. Clear terms, no surprises."
  description="DummyLead Refund & Cancellation Policy: how the per-seed subscription is billed, how to cancel, and when refunds apply."
>
  <h2>1. Subscription billing</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead is a recurring subscription billed in advance, priced per
    concurrent active seed per month, at the rates on our
    <a href="/#pricing">pricing</a> page. Each billing cycle is charged through
    our payment processor at the start of the cycle. By subscribing you authorize
    these recurring charges until you cancel.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Adding and retiring seeds</h2>
  <p>
    You can add or retire seeds at any time from your dashboard. Changes apply
    immediately and are <strong>prorated</strong> to your current billing cycle:
    adding seeds adds a prorated charge, and retiring seeds reduces what counts
    toward your next renewal. Only concurrent active seeds count toward your bill.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Cancellation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can cancel at any time from your dashboard or by emailing
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Cancellation stops future renewals. Your subscription stays active until
      the end of the cycle you have already paid for, and you keep access until
      then.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do not charge a cancellation fee, and we do not lock you into a fixed
      term unless you have separately agreed to an annual or custom contract in
      writing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Because DummyLead delivers a usage-based service that we provision as soon as
    your seeds go live, fees are generally <strong>non-refundable</strong>, and
    we do not provide prorated refunds for partial billing periods after a
    cancellation takes effect. The following exceptions apply:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing errors.</strong> If you were charged in error, for example
      a duplicate charge or a charge after a confirmed cancellation, we will
      refund the incorrect amount.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service failure.</strong> If a sustained fault on our side prevents
      the service from working and we cannot resolve it in a reasonable time, we
      will, at our discretion, issue a credit or a refund for the affected
      period.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Where required by law.</strong> Nothing in this policy limits any
      non-waivable refund or cancellation right you have under applicable
      consumer-protection law where you live.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> from the address on your account
    within <strong>30 days</strong> of the charge, with your account details and
    the reason for the request. We aim to review requests within five business
    days. Approved refunds are returned to your original payment method through
    our payment processor; the time it takes to appear depends on your bank or
    card issuer.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Chargebacks</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe a charge is wrong, please contact us first, we can almost
    always resolve it faster than a chargeback. Filing a chargeback without
    contacting us may result in suspension of your account while the dispute is
    investigated.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Failed payments</h2>
  <p>
    If a payment fails, we may retry it and will notify you. If it remains unpaid,
    we may suspend or downgrade your account until the balance is settled. Your
    data is retained as described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>
    during any suspension.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. Changes take effect on the
    updated effective date above and apply to billing cycles that begin after
    that date.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Billing questions: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. This policy works
    alongside our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Not legal advice.</strong> The consumer laws of the places where
      you sell may grant rights this policy cannot override. Have an attorney
      confirm your refund obligations before publishing.
    </p>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
